    COMMENT: ====================================================================================
    COMMENT: CUSTOM PROPERTIES FOR SaveSlot OBJECT
    COMMENT: ====================================================================================

    PUBLIC source: String
        PURPOSE: Names which copy of this slot you are currently looking at, "cloud" or "local", or "conflict" when both copies hold a save and the local one is newer
        WHY: A save slot is intended to be stored on the cloud, with a local fallback protecting it from network loss and server outages. Either copy can be the one being described, and a game needs to know which so it can show players whether a save has reached the cloud yet
        DEFAULT: "cloud"

        COMMENT: This is NOT part of any component result, and it must stay OUT of
        COMMENT: propertyNames. That list drives toObject(), whose output becomes the
        COMMENT: request payload, so listing it here would ship it to the gateway as a
        COMMENT: parameter no component accepts.
        COMMENT:
        COMMENT: AppState sets this to "local" when the locally mirrored copy is fresher
        COMMENT: and wins the merge, and saveDataRaw()/clearData() set it when a write
        COMMENT: reaches local storage but not the cloud. AppState sets it to "conflict"
        COMMENT: when the local copy is newer but the cloud holds a save too: the slot's
        COMMENT: fields then describe the cloud copy, getLocalCopy() describes the local
        COMMENT: one, and loading returns the local copy until keepLocal() or keepCloud().
        COMMENT: clearSessionData() resets it to "cloud", since the local copy belongs to
        COMMENT: the player who signed out. See AppState's save slot local fallback.
